# 24. A Practical Exercise

For your Week 2 Rust learning, I recommend building this:

## Student Management System

Create:

```rust
struct Student {
    id: u32,
    name: String,
    age: u8,
    course: String,
    score: f64,
}
```

Then implement:

```rust
impl Student {
    fn new(
        id: u32,
        name: String,
        age: u8,
        course: String,
        score: f64,
    ) -> Student {
        Student {
            id,
            name,
            age,
            course,
            score,
        }
    }

    fn display(&self) {
        println!("ID: {}", self.id);
        println!("Name: {}", self.name);
        println!("Age: {}", self.age);
        println!("Course: {}", self.course);
        println!("Score: {}", self.score);
    }

    fn is_passed(&self) -> bool {
        self.score >= 50.0
    }
}
```

Then:

```rust
fn main() {
    let student = Student::new(
        1,
        String::from("John"),
        22,
        String::from("Computer Science"),
        75.5,
    );

    student.display();

    println!("Passed: {}", student.is_passed());
}
```

