# 25. What You Should Be Able to Do Before Moving On

Don't just memorize the definition of a struct. By the end of this topic, you should be comfortable doing these without copying code:

### Beginner level

- [ ] Define a struct
- [ ] Create a struct instance
- [ ] Access fields
- [ ] Modify fields
- [ ] Make a struct mutable
- [ ] Pass a struct to a function
- [ ] Borrow a struct with `&`

### Intermediate level

- [ ] Create methods using `impl`
- [ ] Understand `&self`
- [ ] Understand `&mut self`
- [ ] Understand `self`
- [ ] Create associated functions such as `new()`
- [ ] Use tuple structs
- [ ] Understand struct ownership

### Backend level

- [ ] Derive `Debug`
- [ ] Derive `Serialize`
- [ ] Derive `Deserialize`
- [ ] Understand request structs
- [ ] Understand response structs
- [ ] Understand database/model structs
- [ ] Understand nested structs
- [ ] Understand why different layers may use different structs

